SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Gobierno de México garantiza bienestar y gobernabilidad, afirma presidente en 4° aniversario del triunfo de la 4T en elecciones","publisher":"Presidencia de México","publication_date":"2022-07-01","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/gobierno-de-mexico-garantiza-bienestar-y-gobernabilidad-afirma-presidente-en-4-aniversario-del-triunfo-de-la-4t-en-elecciones/","claim":"AMLO framed the 4T as a government focused on welfare for the whole population, especially the neediest, and said governability and peace remained priorities.","locator":"opening paragraphs / quoted speech","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential transcript; strong for stated program and revealed priorities, though self-presenting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's own articulated program.","contrary_evidence":["It states intent and self-description, not verified implementation or impact."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.3","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Comunicado No. 052 Secretaría de Hacienda y Crédito Público entrega Paquete Económico 2022 al Congreso","publisher":"Secretaría de Hacienda y Crédito Público","publication_date":"2021-09-08","url":"https://www.gob.mx/shcp/prensa/comunicado-no-052-secretaria-de-hacienda-y-credito-publico-entrega-paquete-economico-2022-al-congreso","claim":"The 2022 budget package was designed around social welfare, regional projects, and fiscal stability, with higher programmed spending for social protection, investment, health, education, and more stable debt.","locator":"bullet list under 'tres pilares' and spending paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget document from the finance ministry; strong for declared priorities and resource allocation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"It sets the 2022 policy framework and funding priorities used during the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's administration through the federal budget process.","contrary_evidence":["It is a plan and allocation statement, not proof that all spending translated into effective delivery."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Comunicado No. 39 El Gobierno Federal presenta la Política de Bienestar al Salario de las y los Maestros","publisher":"Secretaría de Hacienda y Crédito Público","publication_date":"2022-05-16","url":"https://www.gob.mx/shcp/prensa/comunicado-no-39?idiom=es-MX","claim":"The federal government unveiled a salary-wellbeing policy for more than 1.18 million education workers, prioritizing lower-income teachers and estimating about 25 billion pesos in funding.","locator":"opening summary and bullet points","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary announcement from the finance ministry, directly tied to the president and the education budget.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's government decisions on wages and education spending.","contrary_evidence":["It does not by itself establish long-run learning gains or whether the wage policy solved teacher deployment problems."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Comunicado No. 37 Presenta el secretario de Hacienda el Paquete Contra la Inflación y la Carestía","publisher":"Secretaría de Hacienda y Crédito Público","publication_date":"2022-05-04","url":"https://www.gob.mx/shcp/prensa/comunicado-no-37-presenta-el-secretario-de-hacienda-el-paquete-contra-la-inflacion-y-la-carestia","claim":"The PACIC was launched to stabilize prices for 24 basic food items and raise domestic food production instead of using a formal price-control regime.","locator":"opening paragraph and policy summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government record of the anti-inflation package and its stated mechanism.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's administration and its inflation-response strategy.","contrary_evidence":["The effectiveness of the package had to be judged against later inflation outcomes and fiscal cost."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Acceso a la atención médica gratuita, prioridad del modelo de salud IMSS-Bienestar: Alcocer","publisher":"Secretaría de Salud","publication_date":"2022-06-16","url":"https://www.gob.mx/salud/prensa/acceso-a-la-atencion-medica-gratuita-prioridad-del-modelo-de-salud-imss-bienestar-alcocer?idiom=es-MX","claim":"The health ministry said 15 states had completed the federalization data-gathering process for IMSS-Bienestar and that 10,920 doctors had been recruited to support free care, equipment, and medicines.","locator":"mid-article paragraphs on state participation and staffing","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ministry announcement with concrete operational metrics and rollout detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's health-system rollout and federalization agenda.","contrary_evidence":["It is a rollout statement; it does not alone prove system-wide quality or equal coverage."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.4","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Se instala Junta de Gobierno del IMSS-Bienestar","publisher":"Secretaría de Salud","publication_date":"2022-09-20","url":"https://www.gob.mx/salud/prensa/se-instala-junta-de-gobierno-del-imss-bienestar-314989","claim":"The IMSS-Bienestar board was installed and the new OPD began legal and juridical operations after the 31 August 2022 decree, formalizing the federalized health model.","locator":"opening summary and first paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary institutional record showing formal launch and governance setup.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's government; this is an implementation and institutionalization step, not just rhetoric.","contrary_evidence":["The source proves formal launch, not full national execution quality."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Boletín SEP no. 24 Reciben programas educativos incremento presupuestal para 2022: Delfina Gómez Álvarez","publisher":"Secretaría de Educación Pública","publication_date":"2022-01-29","url":"https://www.gob.mx/sep/articulos/boletin-sep-no-24-reciben-programas-educativos-incremento-presupuestal-para-2022-delfina-gomez-alvarez?idiom=es","claim":"The SEP said 2022 education programs received higher budgets, including a 13.7% increase for La Escuela es Nuestra, a 4% increase for Benito Juárez scholarships, and more funding for special education.","locator":"first bullets under 'acciones estratégicas'","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary education-ministry budget announcement with concrete program-level funding changes.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's budgetary priorities and education implementation.","contrary_evidence":["Budget increases do not by themselves prove learning or equity gains."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Comunicado de prensa 003/2022 Madres y padres de familia son quienes deciden el uso de los recursos de La Escuela es Nuestra","publisher":"Secretaría de Educación Pública","publication_date":"2022-04-29","url":"https://www.gob.mx/sep/en/articulos/comunicado-de-prensa-003-2022-madres-y-padres-de-familia-son-quienes-deciden-el-uso-de-los-recursos-de-la-escuela-es-nuestra","claim":"La Escuela es Nuestra delivered funds directly to school parent committees, which decide use for construction, maintenance, equipment, longer hours, or student feeding.","locator":"opening summary and bullet points","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary program rule announcement with clear delivery mechanism and local implementation design.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's delivery model for education spending.","contrary_evidence":["Direct community control can improve reach, but the source itself does not measure outcomes."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Resultados demuestran que México está saliendo adelante, afirma presidente en Cuarto Informe de Gobierno","publisher":"Presidencia de México","publication_date":"2022-09-01","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/resultados-demuestran-que-mexico-esta-saliendo-adelante-afirma-presidente-en-cuarto-informe-de-gobierno/","claim":"The president reported that by 2022 La Escuela es Nuestra had reached about 66% of basic schools with maintenance budgets, IMSS-Bienestar had been installed in three states, and medicine availability in those states had reached 95%.","locator":"result sections on education and health","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official results report with concrete implementation metrics; self-reported but specific and contemporaneous.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's administration, though the report is self-evaluative.","contrary_evidence":["This is a government self-report and should be corroborated against independent evaluations where possible."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"21.03.22 Versión estenográfica. Recepción e inicio de operaciones del Aeropuerto Internacional Felipe Ángeles","publisher":"Presidencia de México","publication_date":"2022-03-21","url":"https://amlo.presidente.gob.mx/21-03-22-version-estenografica-recepcion-e-inicio-de-operaciones-del-aeropuerto-internacional-felipe-angeles/","claim":"AMLO said the AIFA opened on time and within the original budget, presenting it as a major infrastructure delivery achieved despite legal, technical, pandemic, and supply-chain constraints.","locator":"central opening paragraphs on budget, timing, and construction progress","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential transcript documenting the launch and the administration's own delivery claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's own infrastructure program and the government's execution claim.","contrary_evidence":["The source is self-reporting and does not by itself establish demand or operational success after opening."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"En medio de dudas, presidente mexicano inaugura nuevo aeropuerto","publisher":"Infobae / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-21","url":"https://www.infobae.com/america/agencias/2022/03/21/en-medio-de-dudas-presidente-mexicano-inaugura-nuevo-aeropuerto/","claim":"Reuters reported that the AIFA opened with only a handful of flights and without a rail connection, even though it was meant to ease congestion at Mexico City's airport.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting republished by Infobae; strong for operational caveats at inauguration, though not a full performance audit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's flagship project at launch, though the low-traffic issue partly reflects start-up conditions and logistics.","contrary_evidence":["A new airport can open before full traffic ramps up, so this is an early-warning indicator rather than final failure."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico's Pemex requests $6.5 billion more funding for 'Dos Bocas' refinery -documents, source","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-12","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/mexicos-pemex-requests-65-billion-more-funding-for-dos-bocas-refinery--documents-source-2871661?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters reported that Dos Bocas needed almost $6.5 billion more in funding, pushing the projected cost to about $14.6 billion, far above the original budget.","locator":"opening paragraphs on the funding request and revised cost estimate","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting based on documents and sources; strong on cost escalation, though the piece is not an audit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's signature energy project and the administration's execution choices, though higher costs also reflect project complexity and inflation.","contrary_evidence":["The story does not prove the project was doomed; it does show serious cost overrun and scope pressure."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexican president's contentious electricity overhaul defeated in Congress","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-04-17","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/commodities-news/mexican-lawmakers-to-vote-on-presidents-contentious-electricity-overhaul-2804968","claim":"AMLO's plan to increase state control of power generation was defeated in parliament after opposition parties argued it would hurt investment and breach international obligations.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on a concrete legislative defeat and the stated investor concerns.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to AMLO's policy push, though legislative defeat also reflects opposition strength and coalition limits.","contrary_evidence":["Defeat in Congress is not the same as administrative incompetence, but it does show failure to convert the proposal into law."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.5","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release and Staff Report","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-11-04","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/11/04/mexico-2022-article-iv-consultation-press-release-and-staff-report-525448","claim":"The IMF said Mexico's recovery was slower than many peers, inflation had become more entrenched, financial conditions had tightened, and the country still faced long-standing low growth and inequality problems.","locator":"summary section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent Article IV surveillance with country-specific macro assessment and direct policy commentary.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly attributable to AMLO's administration in combination with external shocks and inherited constraints; not all macro weakness is ruler-caused.","contrary_evidence":["The IMF did not describe a macro crisis or collapse; it described gradual recovery with persistent structural weaknesses."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.9","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"OECD Economic Surveys: Mexico 2022","publisher":"OECD","publication_date":"2022-02","url":"https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/2022/02/oecd-economic-surveys-mexico-2022_a2937d37.html","claim":"The OECD said uncertainty rose after electricity-market reform proposals, investment had been weak since 2015, and investors needed certainty about contracts and regulatory stability to restart growth.","locator":"summary text near the discussion of investment and electricity reform","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent economic survey with direct policy diagnosis and investment assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to the 2022 policy environment.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to AMLO's policy program and the uncertainty it created, though some investment weakness predates his term.","contrary_evidence":["The OECD also acknowledged Mexico's solid macro framework, so the picture is mixed rather than uniformly negative."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.5","8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Banco Mundial y México colaboran para impulsar el crecimiento económico inclusivo y sostenible","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-05-31","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/05/31/banco-mundial-y-mexico-colaboran-para-impulsar-el-crecimiento-economico-inclusivo-y-sostenible","claim":"The World Bank approved a US$700 million operation tied to policies that simplify the business environment, promote financial inclusion, strengthen sustainable economic management, and help vulnerable groups benefit from growth.","locator":"opening paragraphs and quoted remarks from the World Bank director","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent development-finance approval with explicit policy linkages and targeted objectives.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to AMLO's policy agenda as adopted by the government, though the operation is a partnership and not a ruler-only achievement.","contrary_evidence":["The approval confirms a policy framework, not final results."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mexico anti-inflation subsidies come with $28 billion price tag","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-08-02","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/mexico-antiinflation-subsidies-come-with-28-billion-price-tag-2860789","claim":"Reuters reported that Mexico's anti-inflation subsidies cost about 575 billion pesos in 2022, mostly through gasoline support, and officials said inflation would have been 2.6 percentage points higher without them.","locator":"opening paragraphs and finance-ministry remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with concrete fiscal and inflation claims; the exact counterfactual estimate is official and should be treated cautiously.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to AMLO's crisis-management strategy, though the inflation environment was also driven by global shocks.","contrary_evidence":["Heavy subsidies have fiscal costs and do not demonstrate durable price control by themselves."],"lenses":["8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I considered roughly 30 to 40 documents across AMLO's official 2022 speeches and reports, SHCP/SEP/Salud implementation notices, IMF/OECD/World Bank surveillance, and Reuters/Infobae/Forbes/Bloomberg Línea reporting.
- I kept sources that linked AMLO's program to concrete budgets, institutional rollout, completed projects, or independently described outcomes.
- I rejected repeated social-program pages that restated the same beneficiary counts without adding a new implementation mechanism or outcome.
- I rejected broad Mexico macro or poverty explainers when they did not add ruler-period attribution beyond what the IMF/OECD/World Bank sources already provided.
- I rejected later 2023 or 2024 follow-ups when the 2022 source already captured the relevant implementation or failure.
- I rejected articles that only restated that Mexico had low growth, high corruption, or institutional weakness without connecting those conditions to AMLO's own program choices or execution.
- I also rejected some infrastructure commentary that was too speculative about eventual completion to add more than the AIFA and Dos Bocas pieces already included.

**Remaining Gaps**
- The main unresolved question is durability: 2022 shows large-scale mobilization, but the evidence is thinner on whether the flagship infrastructure and social programs produced lasting productivity gains by year-end.
- More independent evaluation of LEEN, IMSS-Bienestar, and PACIC would help separate real operational delivery from official self-reporting.
- The clearest weaknesses are still investment climate, energy-policy uncertainty, and cost overruns on flagship projects; stronger evidence on how much of that was AMLO's direct control versus inherited constraints would improve attribution.
- I still do not have a clean, ruler-specific causal chain from the 2022 anti-inflation package to household welfare net of fiscal cost and macro side effects.
- If you want this chapter judged later, the next highest-value search would be independent audits or evaluations of AIFA, Dos Bocas, IMSS-Bienestar, and the education program results after the 2022 rollout.
